The residual identifies a static-sort issue, not a missing program rule: the backend split the outer sequence into a generic `Val` head but did not refine the digit-string predicate into the `str` subsort, so method dispatch explored irrelevant list/ref cases. Following the Kit’s sequence-domain guidance, I’m replacing that general loop claim with constructor-exposed empty/cons obligations. Together they still cover every finite list, and they avoid adding any cast or operational bridge.
