The depth-220 trace confirms the remaining issue occurs on the second symbolic list element: the predicate is true, but K still keeps its head at sort `Val`. I’m applying the Kit’s guarded total-projection pattern now. The projection is exact on `str(CS)`, opaque off-domain, and every count-dispatch twin is guarded by the existing string predicate and restates the supplied `str.count` equation; no call/control/state execution is skipped.
